== 4.8 Chapter 4 Practice Drill — 40 Questions

40 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 44 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [The functional group of an ester is],
  [–OH],
  [–CHO],
  [–COOH],
  [–COO–]
)

#mcq(2, [The ester formed from ethanol and ethanoic acid is],
  [ethyl ethanoate],
  [ethanoic anhydride],
  [methyl ethanoate],
  [ethyl methanoate]
)

#mcq(3, [The reaction between an alcohol and a carboxylic acid is called],
  [polymerisation],
  [esterification],
  [hydrolysis],
  [saponification]
)

#mcq(4, [Concentrated sulphuric acid is used in esterification because it],
  [dissolves the ester],
  [acts as an oxidising agent],
  [catalyses the reaction and removes the water],
  [neutralises the acid]
)

#mcq(5, [Esters are responsible for],
  [the sour taste of vinegar],
  [the colour of leaves],
  [the smell of rotten eggs],
  [the pleasant smell of fruit]
)

#mcq(6, [A fat or an oil is an ester of],
  [glucose and a fatty acid],
  [glycerol and three fatty acids],
  [ethanol and a fatty acid],
  [glycerol and three mineral acids]
)

#mcq(7, [Oils are liquid at room temperature while fats are solid because oils],
  [have shorter chains only],
  [contain glycerol],
  [are made from animals],
  [contain unsaturated chains with kinks that prevent close packing]
)

#mcq(8, [The process of converting a liquid oil into a solid fat is],
  [saponification],
  [oxidation],
  [hydrogenation],
  [esterification]
)

#mcq(9, [The catalyst used in the hydrogenation of vegetable oil is],
  [vanadium(V) oxide],
  [iron],
  [nickel],
  [phosphoric acid]
)

#mcq(10, [Soap is made by boiling a fat with],
  [concentrated sodium hydroxide],
  [sodium chloride solution],
  [concentrated sulphuric acid],
  [dilute hydrochloric acid]
)

#mcq(11, [The process of making soap from a fat is called],
  [saponification],
  [fermentation],
  [hydrogenation],
  [esterification]
)

#mcq(12, [The other product formed, besides soap, when a fat is boiled with alkali is],
  [water],
  [ethanol],
  [glycerol],
  [carbon dioxide]
)

#mcq(13, [The ionic head of a soap molecule is],
  [the hydrocarbon chain],
  [the ester group],
  [the carboxylate group, –COO⁻],
  [the amino group]
)

#mcq(14, [Soap removes grease by],
  [dissolving it in water],
  [oxidising it],
  [neutralising it],
  [forming micelles that lift it into the water]
)

#mcq(15, [Soap forms a scum in hard water because],
  [soap is an acid],
  [soap is not soluble in water],
  [hard water is acidic],
  [the calcium and magnesium salts of the fatty acids are insoluble]
)

#mcq(16, [Detergents lather in hard water because],
  [they contain no hydrocarbon chain],
  [they are strong alkalis],
  [they contain soap],
  [their calcium salts are soluble]
)

#mcq(17, [The environmental problem associated with branched-chain detergents is that they],
  [make water hard],
  [are poisonous to fish],
  [are not readily biodegraded, so they foam in rivers],
  [dissolve glass]
)

#mcq(18, [Phosphates in detergents cause pollution because they],
  [prevent lathering],
  [are toxic to fish],
  [act as nutrients and cause eutrophication],
  [make the water acidic]
)

#mcq(19, [In condensation polymerisation, the monomers must each have],
